hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15797","Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Ibn Abi Hadrad al-Aslami, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking a ruling about the dowry of a woman. He said: How much did you give her as dowry? He said: Two hundred dirhams. He said: Had you been scooping from Bathhan, you would not have added."
"15798","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, he said: Abu Hadrad al-Aslami narrated to us, that a man came and mentioned the like of it."
